{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":420912,"ns":0,"title":"Advanced multi-mission operations system","extract":"The advanced multi-mission operations system (AMMOS) is a common set of services and tools created by the Interplanetary Network Directorate, a division of the Jet Propulsion Laboratory, for use in JPL's operation of spacecraft. These tools include a means by which mission planning and analysis can be undertaken, as well as developing pre-planned command sequences for the spacecraft.","description":"Group of tools for operating spacecraft","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}